# Auth Feature Rules

**Entry:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) · **Standards:** [RULES.md](../../RULES.md) §3.3, §3.5 · **Deep dive:** [docs/ai/06-feature-auth.md](../../docs/ai/06-feature-auth.md)

## Structure

`data/models/` → `data/repos/auth_repo_impl.dart` → `presentation/manager/*_cubit/`

Legacy views under `presentation/views/` — prefer JSON routes for new work.

## Endpoints (ground truth)

| Method | Path |
|--------|------|
| POST | `/api/v1/customer/auth/otp/request` |
| POST | `/api/v1/customer/auth/otp/verify` |

**Wrong:** `/api/v1/auth/otp/*` — do not use.

## Must

- Return `Either<Failure, T>` from repo
- Persist tokens via `AuthTokenStorage` on verify
- Register repos/cubits in `service_locator.dart`
- Session changes via `AuthCubit` / `TokenCubit` + `AuthInterceptor`
- Surface `AuthFailureState` / `AuthOtpRequested` messages via **`AppMessenger`** in `_AuthRequestHost` (`variant_screen.dart`) — not `SnackBar`

## Must not

- Put OTP/business rules only in widgets
- Bypass token storage on verify
- Trust `docs/_archive/` or stubbed feature READMEs for paths
- `ScaffoldMessenger.showSnackBar` for auth feedback

## JSON routes

`/auth/login`, `/auth/otp-reset` — typically in `shellExcludeRoutes` in prod config.
